{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-information.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-weighted-systems.json","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-INFORMATION-BLINDNESS","literal_value":{"distinct_values":57,"groups":80,"local_law_classes":3552,"max_chain_gap":2.4e-15},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Read from the published information table after D0. Not a frozen estimand. The balanced weighting is invariant under vertex permutation and single-bit complement, while the local-law class is invariant only under vertex permutation. The conditional-minus-marginal difference is I(G1;G2|slot,mask), non-negative under this weighting, and is not used as a score.","observable":"I(full current triad ; next pair slot | full pair mask) across systems","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"Generation 8D Round D0, all 3584 W4 weighted two-rule T->P systems at N=4, H=0, balanced weighting where information is named","statement":"The balanced current-triad slot information is constant on 80 groups defined by family, same or different triad, opposite literals on one triad, and the weight multiset. It does not change with vertex placement, action adjacency, action direction, or literal polarity. 3552 S4 local-law classes carry 57 distinct information values. The chain rule I(G1,G2) = I(G1) + I(G2 | G1) holds to 2.4e-15 on all 2608 two-gate systems, and a gate's information given the other gate is never below its marginal.","status":"active","structural_roles":["symmetry","projection_loss"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-round-d0-tables.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-information.json","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-INFORMATION-NOT-DIMENSION","literal_value":{"below_larger_single":64,"dim1_max":0.059365300578680294,"dim2_max":0.04781829997118239,"dim2_min":0.005059081105794422},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"More gates and more effective dimension do not imply more information.","observable":"balanced information against effective gate dimension and rule count","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":5},"scope":"Generation 8D Round D0, all 3584 W4 weighted two-rule T->P systems at N=4, H=0, balanced weighting where information is named","statement":"The largest balanced information in the census, 0.059365300578680294 nats, belongs to a dimension-one complementary two-level law, ORB-0101-W01. The dimension-two maximum is 0.04781829997118239 nats. A gated toggle, a slot-gate XOR, and a switched dimension-two system carry the same 0.046736889544 nats with one, two, and three coordinates. In 64 systems the two-rule information is below the larger single-rule value.","status":"active","structural_roles":["negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"local"}
